114
00:57:43.000 --> 00:58:21.000
country for this generation. And I think he was right, and I think this is the big sort of, as it were, the takeaway from all this. Because the clan was beaten. The clan basically by this point late 1871, 1872, has completely ceased to exist. But it has already achieved most of what it wanted to do. So in some states, the clan made a massive difference. It made an electoral difference. So the Democrats have already regained control, for example, of Georgia and Alabama in 1870. The clan smashed the Republican Party in the South. It destroyed local organizations. It made it impossible to basically be an open Republican.
我认为他是对的，我认为这就是这一切的重大收获。因为三K党被击败了。到1871年底、1872年，三K党基本上已经完全不复存在。但它已经实现了它想要做的大部分事情。所以在一些州，三K党产生了巨大的影响。它产生了选举影响。例如，民主党在1870年已经重新控制了佐治亚州和阿拉巴马州。三K党粉碎了南方的共和党。它摧毁了当地组织。它使得基本上不可能成为一名公开的共和党人。

115
00:58:21.000 --> 00:59:17.000
One Mississippi Republican said, you can't basically have your best and most reliable workers murdered with impunity and hope to function as a democratic organization. And so the South will remain Democrat for decades and decades to come. Exactly. It destroys the institutions of the black freed men and freed women. So their churches, their schools and so on. Don't forget these institutions are so precious because they're so new and because their independence is so fragile. And of course, the other big thing, it does what the Southerners had always planned to do. It destroys the patience and the political will of people in the north. So if you get to like, I don't know, 1872, you are 12 years on from the election of Abraham Lincoln and the outbreak. of the war pretty much. And if you're in the north, you're sitting there in, you know, Illinois or Maine or wherever it might be.
一位密西西比州的共和党人说，你基本上不能让最优秀、最可靠的工人在不受惩罚的情况下被谋杀，还指望能作为一个民主组织运作。因此，南方在未来几十年里将保持民主党阵营。没错。这摧毁了黑人自由民的制度，比如他们的教堂、学校等等。别忘了，这些制度之所以珍贵，是因为它们太新了，而且它们的独立性非常脆弱。当然，另一件大事是，它实现了南方人一直计划做的事情。它摧毁了北方人民的耐心和政治意愿。所以如果你到了，我不知道，1872年，距离亚伯拉罕·林肯当选和战争爆发已经过去了12年。如果你在北方，你坐在伊利诺伊州或缅因州或其他任何地方。

116
00:59:17.000 --> 00:59:32.000
You've got a fat cigar. You've got a top hat. You're making loads of money in railroads. Yeah. Right. And you're thinking to yourself, 12 years now, I've been listening to all this stuff and I'm apps. It's the most boring subjects in the world. It's a little bit when people used to say, we used the Northern Ireland parallel earlier.
你抽着粗雪茄，戴着高礼帽，在铁路生意上赚了大钱。是的，没错。你心里想，12年了，我一直在听这些东西，这简直是世界上最无聊的话题。这有点像人们过去常说的，我们之前用了北爱尔兰的类比。

117
